      "char_count": 1589,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 63,
          "text": "1. Purpose"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 87,
          "text": "This policy establishes the principles, criteria, and controls governing the recognition and measurement of Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 102,
          "text": "Intake across the Company."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 129,
          "text": "2. Scope"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 156,
          "text": "This policy applies to all business units, regions, and legal entities that generate, process, or record customer orders"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 168,
          "text": "under the Order-to-Cash (O2C) cycle, including:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 189,
          "text": "- Hardware and Software arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 207,
          "text": "- Standalone Services arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 222,
          "text": "- Bundled multi-element arrangements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 255,
          "text": "3. Definitions"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 282,
          "text": "3.1 Order"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 303,
          "text": "A binding agreement between the Company and a customer under which the Company commits to deliver goods"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 315,
          "text": "and/or services in exchange for consideration."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 339,
          "text": "3.2 Order Backlog"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 360,
          "text": "The cumulative value of Orders recognized as Order Intake but not yet delivered, fulfilled, or recognized as revenue."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 390,
          "text": "4. Roles and Responsibilities"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "table",
          "top": 411.5,
          "rows": [
            [
              "Role",
              "Responsibility"
            ],
            [
              "Sales Operations",
              "Order capture and documentation collection"
            ],
            [
              "Finance Business Partners",
              "Recognition criteria review"
            ],
            [
              "Finance Manager",
              "Credit risk sign-off (see 5.3)"
            ],
            [
              "Group Finance (Revenue Assurance)",
              "Policy ownership and testing"
            ]
          ],
          "n_rows": 5,
          "n_cols": 2
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 528,
          "text": "5. Order Intake Recognition and Measurement"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 555,
          "text": "5.1 Recognition Criteria for Order Intake"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 576,
          "text": "An order shall be recognized as Order Intake when:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 597,
          "text": "- a) A legally binding contract or Purchase Order (PO) exists, AND"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 615,
          "text": "- b) The order value can be reliably measured."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 630,
          "text": "Orders not meeting both (a) and (b) shall remain in the sales pipeline and shall not be recorded as Order Intake."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 654,
          "text": "5.2 Customer Commitment"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 675,
          "text": "Customer commitment is evidenced by receipt of a signed Purchase Order alone. A countersigned contract is"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 687,
          "text": "preferred but not mandatory, provided the PO specifies:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 708,
          "text": "- Price"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 750,
          "text": "CFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | POL-ORD-001 Page 2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_number": 3,
      "extraction_method": "text",
      "char_count": 1451,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 63,
          "text": "- Quantity"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 81,
          "text": "- Delivery terms"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 105,
          "text": "5.3 Collectability Assessment"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 132,
          "text": "5.3.1 Assessment Basis"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 153,
          "text": "Collectability is assessed based solely on the customer's credit rating at time of order receipt, as classified below:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "table",
          "top": 169.5,
          "rows": [
            [
              "Credit Rating",
              "Risk Classification",
              "Action Required"
            ],
            [
              "A",
              "Low Risk",
              "None"
            ],
            [
              "B",
              "Medium Risk",
              "Standard booking"
            ],
            [
              "Below B",
              "High Risk",
              "Finance Manager review"
            ]
          ],
          "n_rows": 4,
          "n_cols": 3
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 261,
          "text": "5.3.2 Escalation Requirements"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 282,
          "text": "Orders from customers rated below \"B\" require Finance Manager sign-off prior to booking. No additional escalation is"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 297,
          "text": "required regardless of order value."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 321,
          "text": "5.4 Timing for Booking of Order Intake"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 339,
          "text": "Order Intake shall be booked immediately upon receipt of a valid Purchase Order, regardless of contract signature"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 354,
          "text": "status. This approach prioritizes:"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 375,
          "text": "- Timeliness of reporting, over"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 390,
          "text": "- Administrative completeness of documentation"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 420,
          "text": "CONTROL PRINCIPLE"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 444,
          "text": "A valid Purchase Order is the primary trigger for Order Intake booking, subject to the recognition criteria and"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 456,
          "text": "collectability requirements defined above."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 489,
          "text": "6. Order Intake Approvals"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 513,
          "text": "Refer to POL-ORD-003 (Order Intake Approval & Backlog Management Policy) for the applicable delegation of"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 528,
          "text": "authority matrix."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 555,
          "text": "7. Exceptions and Escalation"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 579,
          "text": "Deviations from this policy require Finance Manager approval, with escalation to Group Finance for exceptions"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 594,
          "text": "exceeding $100,000 in order value."
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 624,
          "text": "8. Related Policies"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 648,
          "text": "- POL-ORD-002: Order Intake Value & SSP Allocation Policy"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 666,
          "text": "- POL-ORD-003: Order Intake Approval & Backlog Management Policy"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 696,
          "text": "9. Revision History"
        },
        {
          "block_type": "line",
          "top": 750,
          "text": "CFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | POL-ORD-001 Page 3"
        }
      ]
